# RENEX — License Overview

RENEX is published under a **dual-license structure**. Which license applies
to which part depends on the directory:

| Directory / Content | License | File |
|---|---|---|
| `frontend/` (Reference Client, Svelte/Vite) | **MIT OR Apache-2.0** (dual, your choice) | [`LICENSE-MIT`](./LICENSE-MIT), [`LICENSE-APACHE`](./LICENSE-APACHE) |
| `docs/` (Spec, incl. PROTOCOL.md, MULTI_DEVICE.md, RECOVERY.md) | **MIT OR Apache-2.0** (dual, your choice) | [`LICENSE-MIT`](./LICENSE-MIT), [`LICENSE-APACHE`](./LICENSE-APACHE) |
| `src/` (Reference Server, Cloudflare Workers) | **AGPL-3.0-only** | [`LICENSE-AGPL`](./LICENSE-AGPL) |
| `tests/` | same license as the directory being tested | see above |

## Why this split?

- **Spec & Frontend (MIT/Apache)** are meant to spread as widely as possible.
  Anyone should be able to build a RENEX-compatible client — without legal
  friction.
- **Reference Server (AGPL)** prevents hyperscalers from forking the server
  to host their own SaaS versions without contributing improvements back.
  If you operate a RENEX server commercially, you must publish your
  modifications under AGPL.

If you want to write an **alternative** server (from scratch, without
forking our `src/`), you can release it under any license you choose — the
spec itself is permissive.

## Contributor License

All contributions are licensed under the licenses above, depending on the
directory. We use the **Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO)** — every
commit must be signed with `Signed-off-by: Name <email>`.
Details: [`docs/CONTRIBUTING.md`](./docs/CONTRIBUTING.md) §4.

## Trademarks

The name **RENEX** and the RENEX logo are not covered by these licenses.
Forks must not call themselves "RENEX" if this would cause confusion —
please choose a distinct name.

